# Runtime shell assets must stay LF no matter what core.autocrlf a contributor has.
# win-bash-env.sh is sourced by bash (via BASH_ENV) rather than run by Windows, and it
# is copied verbatim into every distributable — a CRLF checkout would ship CRLF. Git
# Bash tolerates the CR, but the GNU bash a WSL user gets does not have to.
backend/src/core/win-bash-env.sh text eol=lf

# The vendored desktop-notification assets are shipped byte-for-byte: the macOS bundle
# carries a code signature that any content rewrite invalidates, the Windows toaster is
# a PE image, and the Windows toast icon has to stay a PNG under the size the toaster
# accepts. Git's content heuristics must not touch any of them.
# The .plist and CodeResources inside the bundle are text but are sealed by the
# signature all the same, so they are covered too. The bundle directory is named after
# the product rather than after upstream's binary — a stale name here protects nothing
# and says nothing about it. README.md and the licence files beside the bundle are ours
# to read and stay normal text.
backend/src/system-notifications/vendor/ntfytoast.exe binary
backend/src/system-notifications/vendor/windows-toast-icon.png binary
"backend/src/system-notifications/vendor/Swttch Notifier.app/**" binary
